Register KVARN_FP16_DEQUANT in envs.py, so the KVarN fp16-dequant switch
(syv-ai/HyperQwen #240) is read through vllm.envs and is part of the
torch.compile cache key (compile_factors() hashes every registered knob that
is not in ignored_factors). Default off ("0"); "1" runs the dequant math of the
three fused KVarN decode kernels in fp16. The kernels and the drivers that read
the knob are in kvarn/files (the kvarn-modules commit on this branch).

Applied after kvarn-0.30.0, kvarn-v2-runner-0.30.0 and
kvarn-recycled-pages-0.30.0. Both hunks sit at the ends of the TYPE_CHECKING block
and of environment_variables, away from kvarn-0.30.0's KVARN_* block, so every
KVarN patch still reverse-applies on its own in a fully installed tree (the
idempotence check patches/apply.sh --kvarn and verify.sh rely on).

--- exported from cpuchip/vllm 7f8c3ef0a (kvarn-fp16-dequant-0.30.0); regenerate with scripts/export-patch.sh, do not edit ---

